.\" Manpage for system-update-notify
.TH SYSTEM-UPDATE-NOTIFY 1 "2026" "awesome-updater 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
system-update-notify \- show system-update attention notifications
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B system-update-notify
.RI [ MODE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B system-update-notify
reads the shared attention state written by
.BR system-update (1)
and displays notifications to the user.
.PP
The helper never modifies system configuration. It only reads the state
file and prints or sends notifications.
.SH MODES
.TP
.B \-\-tty
Print an ANSI-formatted notification to stdout if attention is required.
This is the default mode and is used by
.IR /etc/profile.d/99-system-update.sh .
.TP
.B \-\-gui
Send a single desktop notification using
.BR notify-send (1)
if attention is required. Silently does nothing if
.B notify-send
is unavailable.
.TP
.B \-\-gui-watch
Watch the state file and send a desktop notification whenever the
meaningful state changes. Intended to run inside a desktop session via
XDG autostart.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a short usage message and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/system-update/attention.state
State file read by this helper.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR system-update (1),
.BR notify-send (1)
.SH AUTHOR
megvadulthangya